now you may recall that shea stepped  down as ceo of zappos earlier this year  but  for years he was a driving force in the  revitalization of downtown las vegas  those impacted by his passing are now  trying to find ways to honor what he did  for this city  8 news now reporter madison kimbrough  live from the zappos headquarters  with details on a petition created in  his honor  madison  [Music]  yes a new petition has been circulating  the web getting the attention of las  vegas officials  and we spoke to the man who started it  all  las vegas still reeling over the passing  of entrepreneur and las vegas resident  tony shea several local business owners  speaking out  about their experiences with shea and  all he did for the downtown area of the  city  but one man took it a step further and  created a petition on change.org  his mission renamed part of sixth street  to tony shea way  the man johnny moscow a former las vegas  local  who now lives in honolulu hawaii heard  the news of his passing and knew he had  to do something  i saw the impact that he made on not  just our city but  the first thing that hit me was wow like  the impact that he made on  my my my close family friends the  change.org petition that was just posted  a couple days ago  has already reached its goal of over 2  500 signatures  i think it would be appropriate just to  name it north of fremont where he had  the most impact around the zappos and  downtown  las vegas area so a building i don't  think would keep the  lasting legacy that he's created and las  vegas mayor carolyn goodman agrees that  something should be named in his honor  maybe a park or an art installation  something fitting of a man who had such  a profound  impact on so many people like kathy  brooks  i don't know that i ever really told him  how grateful i was that's what i've been  thinking about this weekend  i know i thanked him but i don't know  that i ever really fully expressed to  him how grateful i am  brooks owns the hydrant club a dog  training center right off of ninth  street and fremont  she accredits shea for giving her the  courage to live out her dream  and leave the tech world behind it's  just wrong that he's gone  he's too young it's too soon look at all  that he accomplished already and i think  about  what could have been possible  and johnny moscow says he hopes that the  petition makes enough  of an impact that something will happen  but of course  that will be up to las vegas officials  what you're looking out now is a  memorial right here  at zappos now carolyn goodman the mayor  obviously  is probably going to discuss this at  wednesday's city council meeting so we  will look out for that  reporting live from zappos madison  kimbrough 8 news now
 

